{#
  Shared overseas-reprocessing-site (ORS) rows for the select-overseas-sites
  page.

  RA-603 T03: this page shows the same ORS row in four sections (accredited,
  registered, new, registered-sites-added). They differ only in their
  data-testid prefixes and in which action the row offers, so before RA-603
  the same ~30 lines of markup existed four times over and every change had to
  be made four times. One macro, four call sites, one place to change.

  Why a table and not govuk-summary-list. A summary list has no real columns:
  each row sizes itself, so a site name in one row cannot line up with the site
  name in the next. The previous markup faked columns with flexbox - `order`,
  a `min-width: 3ch` ORS-id shim and `margin-left: auto` on the actions - and
  still did not align, because `align-items: center` drags a short "Change"
  link out of line with the taller warning button beside it. A table gives the
  browser real columns it sizes consistently across every row, top-aligns cells
  by default, and needs none of that CSS. It also gives the interim accordion a
  valid home: a full-width colspan row directly beneath its parent ORS, which a
  <dl> could never legally contain.

  RA-603 T05/AC10: an ORS's interim sites render in that colspan row behind a
  single "Show interim sites (n)" disclosure, which opens to one line per
  interim site. See interimSiteDisclosure below for why this is govuk-details
  rather than govuk-accordion.

  Emits one or two <tr>, so it must be called from inside a <tbody>.

  Params:
    site           (object, required) - the view-model site. Carries
                   `interimSites` (always an array, see the controller's
                   normaliseInterimSites), plus editUrl/promoteUrl.
    readOnly       (boolean) - hides every action when true, and drops the
                   action column
    crumb          (string) - CSRF token for the POST forms
    testIdPrefix   (string) - e.g. 'accredited-site'; drives the row/name/
                   orsid/country testids
    editTestId     (string) - e.g. 'edit-button-accredited'
    removeFormTestId (string) - e.g. 'remove-form-accredited'
    removeTestId   (string) - e.g. 'remove-button-accredited'
    removeAction   (string) - submitAction value, e.g. 'removeAccredited'
    promote        (boolean) - render the "Add to application" link instead of
                   the Change/Withdraw pair (the registered-only section)
    promoteTestId  (string) - e.g. 'add-button-registered'
    labels         (object) - pre-translated strings, matching how every other
                   component here takes copy. Keys: change, withdraw, add,
                   interimRemove, interimDisclosure
#}

{% macro interimSiteDisclosure(params) %}
  {% set site = params.site %}
  {#
    One disclosure per ORS, not one per interim site. Collapsed, an ORS shows
    a single "Show interim sites (n)" link and nothing else; opened, it shows
    one line per interim site.

    This is govuk-details, not govuk-accordion. The accordion always injects
    its own "Show all sections" control and a header per section, which is
    exactly what this is not meant to look like. Details is a native
    <details>/<summary>, so it also needs no JavaScript to work.
  #}
  <details class="govuk-details select-overseas-sites-interim-disclosure"
           data-testid="interim-sites-disclosure-{{ site.siteId }}">
    <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
      <span class="govuk-details__summary-text" data-testid="interim-sites-disclosure-summary-{{ site.siteId }}">
        {{ params.labels.interimDisclosure }} ({{ site.interimSites.length }})
      </span>
    </summary>
    <div class="govuk-details__text">
      <ul class="govuk-list select-overseas-sites-interim-list">
        {% for interimSite in site.interimSites %}
          {#
            While an ORS can hold only one interim site, the first entry keeps
            the parent-ORS-keyed testids the existing e2e suite already targets.
            Any additional entry is keyed by the interim site's own id, which is
            unique application-wide. That keeps this markup correct for many
            interim sites without breaking the suite before it has been updated.
          #}
          {% set suffix = site.siteId if loop.first else 'is' ~ interimSite.siteId %}
          <li class="select-overseas-sites-interim-item" data-testid="interim-site-row-{{ suffix }}">
            <span class="select-overseas-sites-interim-summary">
              <span data-testid="interim-site-name-{{ suffix }}">{{ interimSite.siteName }}</span>{% if interimSite.country %}, <span data-testid="interim-site-country-{{ suffix }}">{{ interimSite.country }}</span>{% endif %}{% if interimSite.operationCodes.length %}, <span data-testid="interim-site-operation-codes-{{ suffix }}">{{ interimSite.operationCodes | join(', ') }}</span>{% endif %}
            </span>
            {% if not params.readOnly %}
              <span class="select-overseas-sites-interim-actions">
                <a href="{{ interimSite.editUrl }}" class="govuk-link"
                   data-testid="change-interim-site-{{ suffix }}">
                  {{ params.labels.change }}
                </a>
                <form method="post" data-testid="remove-form-interim-site-{{ suffix }}">
                  <input type="hidden" name="crumb" value="{{ params.crumb }}">
                  <input type="hidden" name="siteId" value="{{ site.siteId }}">
                  {# RA-603: the interim site's OWN id. Its parent alone no    #}
                  {# longer identifies which one to withdraw.                  #}
                  <input type="hidden" name="interimSiteId" value="{{ interimSite.siteId }}">
                  <button type="submit" name="submitAction" value="removeInterimSite"
                          class="govuk-button govuk-button--warning govuk-!-margin-bottom-0"
                          data-testid="remove-button-interim-site-{{ suffix }}">
                    {{ params.labels.interimRemove }}
                  </button>
                </form>
              </span>
            {% endif %}
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% if not params.readOnly %}
        {# RA-603 AC01: the way an operator adds a second one. Inside the      #}
        {# disclosure, under the list it extends, rather than beside the ORS   #}
        {# row where it would compete with the ORS's own actions.             #}
        <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
          <a href="{{ site.addInterimSiteUrl }}" class="govuk-link"
             data-testid="add-interim-site-{{ site.siteId }}">
            {{ params.labels.addAnotherInterimSite }}
          </a>
        </p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </details>
{% endmacro %}

{#
  RA-603 C4. Withdrawn interim sites, and the way to put one back.

  A second disclosure rather than a "withdrawn" group inside the first: it
  renders nothing at all when nothing has been withdrawn, which is the normal
  case, and it keeps the main list showing only what is actually on the
  application. An ORS that has churned through several interim sites does not
  turn its own list into a log.

  Restoring is in place - the backend clears removedAt and touches nothing else -
  so the site comes back with the site number it always had rather than as a new
  record. That identity link is the thing AC05 exists to protect, and it is why
  re-adding by hand is not an acceptable substitute for this.
#}
{% macro withdrawnInterimSiteDisclosure(params) %}
  {% set site = params.site %}
  {% if site.withdrawnInterimSites.length %}
    <details class="govuk-details select-overseas-sites-interim-disclosure"
             data-testid="withdrawn-interim-sites-disclosure-{{ site.siteId }}">
      <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
        <span class="govuk-details__summary-text"
              data-testid="withdrawn-interim-sites-disclosure-summary-{{ site.siteId }}">
          {{ params.labels.withdrawnDisclosure }} ({{ site.withdrawnInterimSites.length }})
        </span>
      </summary>
      <div class="govuk-details__text">
        <ul class="govuk-list select-overseas-sites-interim-list">
          {% for interimSite in site.withdrawnInterimSites %}
            <li class="select-overseas-sites-interim-item"
                data-testid="withdrawn-interim-site-row-{{ interimSite.siteId }}">
              <span class="select-overseas-sites-interim-summary">
                <span data-testid="withdrawn-interim-site-name-{{ interimSite.siteId }}">{{ interimSite.siteName }}</span>{% if interimSite.country %}, <span>{{ interimSite.country }}</span>{% endif %}
              </span>
              {% if not params.readOnly %}
                <span class="select-overseas-sites-interim-actions">
                  <form method="post" data-testid="restore-form-interim-site-{{ interimSite.siteId }}">
                    <input type="hidden" name="crumb" value="{{ params.crumb }}">
                    <input type="hidden" name="siteId" value="{{ site.siteId }}">
                    <input type="hidden" name="interimSiteId" value="{{ interimSite.siteId }}">
                    <button type="submit" name="submitAction" value="restoreInterimSite"
                            class="govuk-button govuk-button--secondary govuk-!-margin-bottom-0"
                            data-testid="restore-button-interim-site-{{ interimSite.siteId }}">
                      {{ params.labels.restore }}
                    </button>
                  </form>
                </span>
              {% endif %}
            </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}

{% macro overseasSiteRows(params) %}
  {% set site = params.site %}
  {#
    The ORS id cell is always emitted, empty when the site has none - a table
    column has to exist in every row or the columns below it shift. The
    visually-hidden "ORS ID" label the summary-list version carried is gone:
    the column's own <th scope="col"> names it now, and keeping both made a
    screen reader announce it twice.

    The site name keeps `scope="row"` even though the ORS id now precedes it.
    The id is a reference, the name is what identifies the row to someone
    listening to it, and scope="row" does not require the first column.
  #}
  <tr class="govuk-table__row select-overseas-sites-row{% if site.interimSites.length or site.withdrawnInterimSites.length %} select-overseas-sites-row--has-interim{% endif %}"
      data-testid="{{ params.testIdPrefix }}-row-{{ site.siteId }}">
    <td class="govuk-table__cell select-overseas-sites-orsid" data-testid="{{ params.testIdPrefix }}-orsid-{{ site.siteId }}">{{ site.orsId }}</td>
    <th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header select-overseas-sites-name-cell" data-testid="{{ params.testIdPrefix }}-name-{{ site.siteId }}">{{ site.siteName }}</th>
    <td class="govuk-table__cell" data-testid="{{ params.testIdPrefix }}-country-{{ site.siteId }}">{{ site.country }}</td>
    {% if not params.readOnly %}
      <td class="govuk-table__cell select-overseas-sites-actions-cell">
        {% if params.promote %}
          <a href="{{ site.promoteUrl }}" role="button" draggable="false"
             class="govuk-button govuk-button--secondary govuk-!-margin-bottom-0"
             data-module="govuk-button"
             data-testid="{{ params.promoteTestId }}-{{ site.siteId }}">
            {{ params.labels.add }}
          </a>
        {% else %}
          <a href="{{ site.editUrl }}" class="govuk-link"
             data-testid="{{ params.editTestId }}-{{ site.siteId }}">
            {{ params.labels.change }}
          </a>
          <form method="post" style="display:inline" data-testid="{{ params.removeFormTestId }}-{{ site.siteId }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="crumb" value="{{ params.crumb }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="siteId" value="{{ site.siteId }}">
            <button type="submit" name="submitAction" value="{{ params.removeAction }}"
                    class="govuk-button govuk-button--warning govuk-!-margin-bottom-0"
                    data-testid="{{ params.removeTestId }}-{{ site.siteId }}">
              {{ params.labels.withdraw }}
            </button>
          </form>
        {% endif %}
      </td>
    {% endif %}
  </tr>
  {% if site.interimSites.length or site.withdrawnInterimSites.length %}
    <tr class="govuk-table__row select-overseas-sites-interim-tr">
      <td class="govuk-table__cell select-overseas-sites-interim-cell" colspan="{{ 3 if params.readOnly else 4 }}">
        {{ interimSiteDisclosure(params) }}
        {{ withdrawnInterimSiteDisclosure(params) }}
      </td>
    </tr>
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
